.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt P_CANDEBUG 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm p_candebug ,
.Nm p_caninspect
.Nd determine debuggability and inspectability of a process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/proc.h
.Ft int
.Fn p_candebug "struct thread *td" "struct proc *p"
.Ft int
.Fn p_caninspect "struct thread *td" "struct proc *p"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This function determines if a given process
.Fa p
is debuggable by some thread
.Fa td .
.Pp
The following
.Xr sysctl 8
variables directly influence the behaviour of
.Fn p_candebug :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va security.bsd.unprivileged_proc_debug
Must be set to a non-zero value to allow unprivileged processes
access to the kernel's debug facilities.
.It Va kern.securelevel
Debugging of the init process is not allowed if this variable is
.Li 1
or greater.
.El
.Pp
Other such variables indirectly influence it; see
.Xr cr_bsd_visible 9 .
.Pp
The
.Fn p_caninspect
function determines if thread
.Fa td
may inspect process
.Fa p :
see its memory map, auxiliary vector, ps_strings and signal trampoline
locations, signal fast block, umask and kernel stack
.Po
the
.Dv KERN_PROC_VMMAP ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_VM_LAYOUT ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_AUXV ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_PS_STRINGS ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_SIGTRAMP ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_SIGFASTBLK ,
.Dv KERN_PROC_UMASK
and
.Dv KERN_PROC_KSTACK
.Xr sysctl 3
nodes, and the linprocfs
.Pa maps
and
.Pa auxv
files
.Pc .
That is metadata about the process, never the contents of its memory, which
stay under
.Fn p_candebug .
The auxiliary vector is located through pointers in the process's own
memory, so the process controls what an inspector reads as its auxiliary
vector.
.Pp
.Fn p_caninspect
performs the checks of
.Fn p_candebug ,
in the same order and with the same errors, with three differences:
it does not apply a process's software-authority or no-ambient debug
protection (see
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4 ) ,
which protects its memory and control, not its layout;
it asks the MAC policies
.Fn mac_proc_check_inspect
instead of
.Fn mac_proc_check_debug ,
and a policy that does not implement the inspect question answers its
debug question
.Pq see Xr mac 9 ;
and it allows the initial process at any
.Va kern.securelevel .
.Pp
Whoever may debug a process may inspect it:
.Fn p_candebug
returning 0 implies
.Fn p_caninspect
returning 0.
A MAC policy that implements both questions must preserve this.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn p_candebug
and
.Fn p_caninspect
functions
return
.Li 0
if the process denoted by
.Fa p
is debuggable or inspectable, respectively, by thread
.Fa td ,
or a non-zero error return value otherwise.
.Sh ERRORS
Both functions return the following errors, except where noted.
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EPERM
An unprivileged process attempted to debug another process but the system is
configured to deny it
.Po
see
.Xr sysctl 8
variable
.Va security.bsd.unprivileged_proc_debug
above
.Pc .
.It Bq Er ESRCH
Thread
.Fa td
has been jailed and the process to debug does not belong to the same jail or one
of its sub-jails, as determined by
.Xr prison_check 9 .
.It Bq Er ESRCH
.Xr cr_bsd_visible 9
denied visibility according to the BSD security policies in force.
.It Bq Er EPERM
Thread
.Fa td
lacks superuser credentials and its (effective) group set is not a superset of
process
.Fa p Ns 's
whole group set
.Pq "including real, effective and saved group IDs" .
.It Bq Er EPERM
Thread
.Fa td
lacks superuser credentials and its (effective) user ID does not match all user
IDs of process
.Fa p .
.It Bq Er EPERM
Thread
.Fa td
lacks superuser credentials and process
.Fa p
is executing a set-user-ID or set-group-ID executable.
.It Bq Er EPERM
Process
.Fa p
holds a software authority or has no ambient process control
.Pq Dv PD_PROTECTED ,
and thread
.Fa td
may not debug it
.Pq Fn p_candebug No only .
.It Bq Er EACCES
A MAC policy refused the request, for example a
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4
ptrace shield
.Pq Fn p_candebug No only : No the shield does not refuse inspection .
.It Bq Er EPERM
Process
.Fa p
denotes the initial process
.Fn initproc
and the
.Xr sysctl 8
variable
.Va kern.securelevel
is greater than zero
.Pq Fn p_candebug No only .
.It Bq Er EBUSY
Process
.Fa p
is in the process of being
.Fn exec Ns 'ed.
.It Bq Er EPERM
Process
.Fa p
denied debuggability
.Po
see
.Xr procctl 2 ,
command
.Dv PROC_TRACE_CTL
.Pc .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr procctl 2 ,
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4 ,
.Xr cr_bsd_visible 9 ,
.Xr mac 9 ,
.Xr p_cansee 9 ,
.Xr prison_check 9
